{"kind":"finding","date":"2026-11-26","surface":"phone","area":"phone/native","verified":"pending","status":"open","needs_him":false,"proof":"code-read","id":"FN-B-words-phone-native-01","lens":"gap-10","refs":["F-phone-1220"],"severity":"S3","title":"The 'Gym right now' widget tells the member to open the Gym tab, but a tap opens the check-in scanner","what":"When the widget has no fresh reading it says \"Not known yet - Open the Gym tab in MettleUp to see how busy it is\" or \"Check again - Open MettleUp to see how busy it is now\". Tapping anywhere on the widget opens the check-in camera, not the Gym tab, so the step the words give cannot be taken from the widget.","expected":"A tap on a widget that asks the member to look at how busy the gym is opens the Gym tab; or the words say the tap checks you in.","evidence":["apps/mobile/modules/forge-phone/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/phone/Widgets.kt:291-311","apps/mobile/src/tracker/phone/widgets.ts:28"],"root_cause_key":"gym-widget-words-name-other-page","who":"members in a gym who use the 'Gym right now' widget","how_often":"every time the reading is missing or older than its fresh window","fix_line":"When there is no fresh reading, send the tap to the Gym tab, or change the line to say the tap checks you in.","fix_size":"small"}
{"kind":"finding","date":"2026-11-26","surface":"phone","area":"phone/native","verified":"pending","status":"open","needs_him":false,"proof":"code-read","id":"FN-B-words-phone-native-02","lens":"10","refs":["F-phone-1206","F-phone-1208"],"severity":"S4","title":"The same 'tick my next set' button is called 'Done' on the rest card and 'Complete set' on the workout card","what":"During rest the notification button that logs the next set reads \"Done\"; on the live workout card the same action reads \"Complete set\". Android's notification settings describe the rest card as having \"Done\". A member sees two names for one action, sometimes minutes apart.","expected":"One name for the one action on every card (and on the watch).","evidence":["apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/RestCard.kt:913","apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/WorkoutCard.kt:145","apps/mobile/modules/forge-rest/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/rest/RestCard.kt:1307"],"root_cause_key":"two-names-one-set-button","who":"members who log sets from the notification","how_often":"every workout with notifications on","fix_line":"Pick one label (for example \"Complete set\") and use it on both cards and in the channel descriptions.","fix_size":"small"}
{"kind":"finding","date":"2026-11-26","surface":"phone","area":"phone/native","verified":"pending","status":"open","needs_him":false,"proof":"code-read","id":"FN-B-words-phone-native-03","lens":"gap-10","refs":["F-phone-1222"],"severity":"S4","title":"The app-icon shortcut pictures are a flat orange disc, not the shape the launcher expects","what":"\"Start workout\" and \"Log body weight\" on a long-press of the app icon use a plain 48 dp orange circle picture. Android launchers expect an adaptive (full-bleed) shortcut picture and shrink any other kind inside their own plate, so these two can look small and off-style next to other apps' shortcuts. The gym's own home-screen shortcut is already drawn in the adaptive form. Not seen on a phone; read in code.","expected":"Shortcut pictures made in the adaptive form, in the current brand colours.","evidence":["apps/mobile/modules/forge-phone/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/phone/Shortcuts.kt:56","apps/mobile/modules/forge-phone/android/src/main/res/drawable/forge_shortcut_start.xml:1-13","apps/mobile/modules/forge-phone/android/src/main/java/com/forgeai/phone/GymShortcut.kt:55"],"root_cause_key":"shortcut-icons-not-adaptive","who":"members who long-press the app icon","how_often":"every time","fix_line":"Redraw the two shortcut pictures as adaptive icons (like the gym shortcut) from the brand files.","fix_size":"small"}
